Z||000000||reddog||10-19-2001||09:05 PM||||Ok, when I bought my 86GT and got it home I noticed that the EGR tube was off and had not been plugged or anything. Also rear pcv tube was taken out and no grommet on the back valve cover. There was just a big open hole on the back valve cover. I don't know how long the car had been driven in this condition. I have noticed that inside the valve cover at the filler cap there is a thick sludge covering everything.I am getting really bad gas mileage. replaced all emmissions equipment as well as sensors, hoses, ect.What I want to know is is there any thing I can use to flush the sludge out. Also I had read about a professional decarbonizer some where can you tell me what it does how to use it andwhere I can buy it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-19-2001||09:16 PM||||There was a big engine cleaning thread a while ago.  Try a seach for that or kerosene and it should turn up.  Basically, it was about running a solution thru then changing your oil.<BR>Gary<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||10-21-2001||07:39 PM||||There are commercial cleaners you can pour into the crankcase with the oil. My own method is changing the oil, just use cheap oil and make one of the quarts automatic transmission fluid. I drive the car normally just around town for 50-100 miles and drain it. Refill with fresh filter and whatever good oil you prefer. The fluid has lots of cleaning agents in it. Youll see if you ever see the inside of and auto trans.||||reg||1
